Installation Instructions
*************************

EMANE is now built using Rust and Cargo. The legacy GNU Autotools (`configure` / `make`) build system has been removed.

Basic Installation
==================

1. Ensure you have the Rust toolchain, Python 3, pip, setuptools, wheel,
   Protocol Buffers compiler (`protoc`), and the Python `lxml` and `protobuf`
   packages installed.
2. Run the following commands from the root of the repository:

   make prepare-install
   sudo make install

`make prepare-install` performs all compilation as the invoking user: it builds
the release workspace, generates the plugin manifests, builds the Python wheel,
and stages the Python installation. `sudo make install` only copies prepared
artifacts and does not invoke Cargo, `protoc`, or pip as root.

`make install` installs the Rust executables, model plugin libraries, DTD and
schema files, generated plugin manifests, and the Python utilities. A plain
`cargo install` is not sufficient for EMANE because Cargo does not install
workspace `cdylib` plugins or runtime data files.

The default prefix is `/usr`. To install under another prefix:

   make prepare-install PREFIX=/opt/emane
   sudo make install PREFIX=/opt/emane

The executables find plugins relative to that prefix, so `/opt/emane/bin/emane`
will automatically search `/opt/emane/lib/emane`.

Packaging and Staged Installation
=================================

Package builders can stage the installation without writing to the host:

   make prepare-install
   make install DESTDIR=/tmp/emane-package-root PREFIX=/usr
   make installcheck DESTDIR=/tmp/emane-package-root PREFIX=/usr

The resulting layout is:

   PREFIX/bin                  Rust and Python executables
   PREFIX/lib/emane            Rust model plugin libraries
   PREFIX/share/emane/dtd      XML DTDs and entities
   PREFIX/share/emane/schema   XML schemas
   PREFIX/share/emane/manifest generated plugin manifests

`BINDIR`, `LIBDIR`, `DATADIR`, `DTDDIR`, `SCHEMADIR`, and `MANIFESTDIR` can
also be overridden independently for distribution packaging.

Developing and Testing
======================

To run the test suite across the workspace:

   make test

For more information, please consult the EMANE Wiki or the Rust/Cargo documentation.
